    "justification": "The campaign is one accepted, preregistered, single-execution numerical campaign about a declared component model: the accepted L0 conservation model (cft_revival.physics, L0-conservation-reduced-performance) evaluated under the declared multiplicative cusp-survival closure CL-1 and declared uniform priors. That is exactly the object the numerical-campaign gate kind was defined for (one accepted campaign on a declared component model), so the kind is reused with its own typed manifest, evidence file, macro-only section, claim records and campaign checker. Its estimands are properties of the optimisers (hypervolume per budget, Pareto-set size, seed variance, paired comparisons) and of the declared evaluation chain (robust-versus-nominal fronts, sensitivity to the cusp prior). It is optimiser evidence, not performance evidence: it makes no thruster-performance, plasma or physical-device claim, it is not the L1 field-resolved reduction (no field solve, geometry response or L0 mapping), not L2 and not L3, and it therefore opens none of GATE-L1, GATE-L2 or GATE-L3.",
    "name": "numerical-campaign",
    "opens_gate": null,
